  {
   "id": "code_t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 64,
   "y": 874,
   "width": 460.79999999999995,
   "height": 200.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#e2e8f0",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1231,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 5363,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "void sleep_on(void *chan, struct spinlock *lk) {\n    ...\n    if (lk != &sched_lock) {\n        spin_lock(&sched_lock);\n        spin_unlock(lk);\n    }\n    t->chan = chan;\n    t->state = T_SLEEPING;\n    sched();\n    ...",
   "originalText": "void sleep_on(void *chan, struct spinlock *lk) {\n    ...\n    if (lk != &sched_lock) {\n        spin_lock(&sched_lock);\n        spin_unlock(lk);\n    }\n    t->chan = chan;\n    t->state = T_SLEEPING;\n    sched();\n    ...",
   "fontSize": 16,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true,
   "baseline": 14
  },
  {
   "id": "why",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 640,
   "y": 870,
   "width": 384.0,
   "height": 120.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1238,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 5374,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "sleep_on takes sched_lock before it\nreleases the caller's lock. wakeup needs\nsched_lock too, so it cannot run between\nthe sleeper's check of its condition\nand its state becoming SLEEPING.\nThat is what prevents a lost wakeup.",
   "originalText": "sleep_on takes sched_lock before it\nreleases the caller's lock. wakeup needs\nsched_lock too, so it cannot run between\nthe sleeper's check of its condition\nand its state becoming SLEEPING.\nThat is what prevents a lost wakeup.",
   "fontSize": 16,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true,
   "baseline": 14
  }
